# LearnBridge environment variables
#
# Two kinds of value:
#
#   PUBLIC  - safe to commit; visible in the browser. Lovable writes these to .env.
#   SECRET  - never commit. Add them in Lovable: Project settings -> Secrets.
#             They reach server code only, through process.env.
#
# Anything starting with VITE_ is copied into the browser bundle, so it must
# never hold a secret. `npm run check:secrets` enforces this.
#
# Full guide: docs/environments.md

# --- PUBLIC: Lovable Cloud (Supabase) - written by Lovable into .env ---------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-id>.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="<project-id>"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_..."
# The same three values without the VITE_ prefix, for server-side rendering.
SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-id>.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="<project-id>"
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_..."

# --- SECRET: provided at runtime by Lovable Cloud, never in a file -----------
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY     Bypasses row-level security. Server code only.
# LOVABLE_CRON_SECRET           Authenticates scheduled jobs.
# LOVABLE_CRON_SECRET_PREVIOUS  Previous cron secret, kept during rotation.

# --- SECRET: added in later tasks (listed so nobody invents new names) -------
# LIVEKIT_API_KEY / LIVEKIT_API_SECRET / LIVEKIT_URL      Live lessons (P6-01)
# PAYFAST_MERCHANT_ID / PAYFAST_MERCHANT_KEY / PAYFAST_PASSPHRASE / PAYFAST_SANDBOX
#                                                         Payments (P9-03)
# RESEND_API_KEY                                          Email (P4-08)
# SENTRY_DSN                                              Error monitoring (P1-05)
